sub:Head {
    sub: a np:Nanopublication ;
        np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
        np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
        np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila kikkawai Turing wavelength at 2.3 µm (detail, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila kikkawai morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila kikkawai specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Drosophila kikkawai; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) showed a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the activator-substrate kinetics used here. | Gibert, Moreteau & David (1999) showed abdominal pigmentation in D. kikkawai depends on a major gene interacting with sex, segment, and temperature. Yassin et al. (2016) identified pdm3 as a hotspot for female-limited colour dimorphism in Drosophila.; reconstructed_in_script: The 2.343 µm length is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment for slot 3190, realised as the Schnakenberg growth-rate peak at Du=0.020, Dv=1.364, a=0.070, b=0.940. | Predecessor D. hydei (Dv=4.470, λ≈3.056 µm) and successor D. mauritiana (Dv=0.413, λ≈1.820 µm) differ only in inhibitor range. The light/dark major-gene axis is reconstructed as b=0.710 versus b=1.180.; transfer_boundary: The ordering is a property of this dispersion relation at 0 Ma. It is not a measured fossil or morphometric series, and it does not transfer to the 93 µm tergite-band slot.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Gibert et al. or Yassin et al. measured a 2.3 µm pigment wavelength. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a light micrograph of that carrier. Commons returned no D. kikkawai photograph on 2026-10-27. | Does not claim the saturated hero field's FFT peak (2.182 µm) already equals the linear prediction. That gap is remediation R1.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2016.07.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ympev.2020.107061>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1023/a:1003704315194>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

